#!/bin/bash
# The Point Hub board's LED driver, with the tuning from ../setting.ini [DISPLAY]. Geometry is
# compiled into the Piomatter build. Not the C0270's startled: that one needs the vendor's ini parser
# and sudo, and its flags are the hzeller ones.
cd "$(dirname "$0")" || exit 1
ini() { awk -F= -v k="$1" '/^\[/{s=$0} s=="[DISPLAY]" && $1==k {print $2; exit}' ../setting.ini; }
args=("--led-gpio-mapping=$(ini hardware_mapping)" "--led-multiplexing=$(ini multiplexing)"
      "--led-pwm-bits=$(ini pwm_bits)" "--led-pwm-dither-bits=$(ini pwm_dither)"
      "--led-brightness=$(ini brightness)" "--led-rgb-sequence=$(ini rgb_sequence)" --led-no-drop-privs)
for pair in power_budget_ma:--power-budget-ma power_full_white_ma:--power-full-white-ma power_idle_ma:--power-idle-ma; do
  v=$(ini "${pair%%:*}")
  case "$v" in ''|*[!0-9]*) ;; *) args+=("${pair##*:}=$v") ;; esac
done
exec ./flushBuffer2 ../www/buffer.png "${args[@]}"
